---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Configured base without its trailing slash, for prefixing internal links.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Security — 3FA"
  description="3FA's security model, cryptography, and responsible-disclosure policy."
>
  <h1>Security</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    3FA uses client-side vault encryption so the sync service does not need access
    to your OTP seeds. This page separates protections in the current app from
    additional safeguards still under development, and explains how to report a problem.
  </p>

  <h2>Cryptography</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>At rest (implemented):</strong> the desktop vault encrypts OTP seeds using XChaCha20-Poly1305 with passcode-based Argon2id key derivation. Platform Secure Enclave / TPM key wrapping is planned, not implemented.</li>
    <li><strong>In transit / sync:</strong> the entire vault is end-to-end encrypted on your device before upload. The server stores only ciphertext and a version vector — it has no key capable of decrypting it (zero-knowledge).</li>
    <li><strong>Standards:</strong> codes follow RFC 6238 (TOTP) and RFC 4226 (HOTP), verified against the official RFC test vectors.</li>
    <li><strong>Biometrics (not yet available for unlock):</strong> biometric and voice-based factors are planned. The current desktop unlock flow does not collect them as working factors.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Access control</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Current desktop unlock:</strong> a six-digit passcode. A multi-factor policy engine exists, but biometric, passkey, and voice factors are not yet wired into the unlock flow. Configurable 2FA/3FA unlock is not currently available.</li>
    <li><strong>Idle protection:</strong> the desktop app automatically locks after inactivity. Longer idle time conditioned on a second factor is a design goal, not a shipped capability.</li>
    <li>Per-device sync tokens that can be revoked individually.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we can't protect against</h2>
  <p>
    No client software can defend a fully compromised operating system (e.g. a
    kernel-level keylogger active while you unlock) or a coerced user. 3FA limits
    blast radius — it does not claim to be magic.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:security@threefa.app">security@threefa.app</a>. Please
    include reproduction steps and avoid accessing other users' data. We aim to
    acknowledge reports within 72 hours. See our machine-readable policy at
    <a href={`${base}/.well-known/security.txt`}><code>/.well-known/security.txt</code></a>.
  </p>

  <style>
    h2 { margin-top: 40px; }
    ul { color: #c7ccd6; }
    li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    code { background: #1c1c24; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 5px; }
  </style>
</Base>
